> Tada in Lua: short plans that John and an LLM both write
- Format:
  - Lines:
    - [✔] Topics, todos, list items, notes, comments
    - [✔] Metadata sigils
    - [✔] Topics nest 3 deep
    - [✔] Optional header: one note, links
  - Todos:
    - [✔] Four styles: unicode, ascii, simple, markdown
    - [✔] Custom statuses and symbols
    - [✔] Custom colors
  - Dropped:
    - [⚑] Per-file @config
    - [⚑] In-file === archive
          > Archiving moves lines to .tada/archive/
    - [⚑] Todos under todos
          > A todo with children is a topic
- Editing:
  - Todos:
    - [✔] <C-Space> toggles a box
    - [✔] <Space> cycles status
  - Lines:
    - [✔] Enter, o, O continue the line type
    - [✔] Tab indents an empty item
    - [✔] : | > convert an empty line
    - [✔] <C-H> clears left of cursor
  - Movement:
    - [✔] ( ) jump between topics
    - [✔] { } jump between parent topics
    - [✔] Jump from a & link to file:line
  - Metadata:
    - [ ] @: completes assignees from a list
  - Keys:
    - [✔] Move a key or turn it off
- Folds:
  - [✔] Enter folds a topic
  - [✔] <C-T>1-3 fold to a level
  - [✔] <C-T>0 opens all
  - [✔] <C-T>o/c open or close under cursor
  - [✔] Fold text shows todo counts
- Plans:
  - Folder:
    - [✔] Plans live in .tada/
    - [✔] Root Tadafile still opens
  - Pane:
    - [✔] \td opens the last edited plan
    - [✔] Pick another plan from a list
    - [✔] Browse archived plans
  - Archive:
    - [✔] Archive a whole plan
    - [✔] Archive selected lines
          > Appends to the same-named file in archive/
    - [✔] Confirm before archiving a whole plan
  - Commands:
    - [✔] :Tada does what the keys do
- LLM:
  - Skill:
    - [✔] Reads and writes plans
    - [✔] Todos are user stories
    - [✔] Steps only under the active item
    - [✔] Long notes go in .tada/context/, linked with &
    - [✔] Ignores archive/ unless pointed at it
  - Voice:
    - [✔] Good and bad example pairs
    - [⚑] Size test for a draft?
          > A rule of thumb in the skill, not a check
- Release:
  - [✔] 1.0.0 tag pins the Vimscript version
  - [✔] README covers the Lua version
